  "description": "Erection of a single storey rear extension.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "All external facing materials, treatments and finishes shall be similar to those of the original building and maintained and retained thereafter. This applies unless differences are shown on the drawings we have approved. \r\rReason: To ensure that the extension harmonises with the existing building and to ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Fire Safety Statement.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12.",
    "The development hereby approved shall be constructed in accordance with \rthe approved Flood Risk Assessment prepared by Innervison Design Ltd and dated \rJanuary 2026. Prior to first occupation of the extension, documentary evidence that \rthe approved flood resilience and SuDS measures have been implemented must be \rsubmitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing together with \rconfirmation that the development has been registered with the EA's Flood Warning \rService. All of the approved measures must thereafter be retained for as long as the \rdevelopment is in existence. \r\rReason: To comply with Government Standing Advice and Policy 31 of the Sutton \rLocal Plan 2018"
  ],
